    {
      "id": "p1-10",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 0,
      "y": 580.5,
      "width": 418.11944580078125,
      "height": 210.60000000000002,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#5B5B58",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": "frame-0",
      "index": "aG",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 1773849096,
      "version": 2,
      "versionNonce": 1188188168,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": null,
      "updated": 1788177440877,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Every unoffset edge follows the corridor the engine left when it placed\nthe nodes — read back, not redrawn, so no edge here is hand-routed.\nplacement \"straight\" is what lets the handback edge take that corridor\nin two bends instead of three: the engine spends the same bends on\nthe short edges to keep the long one straight, which is the one thing an\noriginAt / landAt cannot buy. What the fractions still do is the engine's\nblind spot — spread the four legs leaving needs-triage across its facing\nedge and move them clear of each other's labels, which ELK spaced its\nports without ever being told about. needs-triage leads because\nmodelOrder makes the order the states were listed in the tie-break,\nand that order picks which edge of the cycle gives way — the picture\nopens where an issue really opens.",
      "fontSize": 13,
      "fontFamily": 6,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Every unoffset edge follows the corridor the engine left when it placed\nthe nodes — read back, not redrawn, so no edge here is hand-routed.\nplacement \"straight\" is what lets the handback edge take that corridor\nin two bends instead of three: the engine spends the same bends on\nthe short edges to keep the long one straight, which is the one thing an\noriginAt / landAt cannot buy. What the fractions still do is the engine's\nblind spot — spread the four legs leaving needs-triage across its facing\nedge and move them clear of each other's labels, which ELK spaced its\nports without ever being told about. needs-triage leads because\nmodelOrder makes the order the states were listed in the tie-break,\nand that order picks which edge of the cycle gives way — the picture\nopens where an issue really opens.",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.35
    },
    {
      "id": "p2-12",
